devices\dev_sgi_gbe.c:158:*
devices\dev_sgi_gbe.c:159:*  frm_control contains a pointer to an array of uint16_t. These numbers
devices\dev_sgi_gbe.c:160:*  (when shifted 16 bits to the left) are pointers to the tiles. Tiles are
devices\dev_sgi_gbe.c:161:*  512x128 in 8-bit mode, 256x128 in 16-bit mode, and 128x128 in 32-bit mode.
devices\dev_sgi_gbe.c:162:*
devices\dev_sgi_gbe.c:163:*  An exception is how Linux/O2 uses the framebuffer, in a "tweaked" mode
devices\dev_sgi_gbe.c:164:*  which resembles linear mode. This code attempts to support both.
devices\dev_sgi_gbe.c:165:*/
