The closest graphics matches use consistent units: VGA has separate 4-bit and 8-bit pixel paths, and the SGI display code converts its bit depth to bytes before testing 1 or 2. I’m extending the check to masked CPU fields and small-constant comparisons to look for dead branches with less obvious names.
